You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task:
You are given a string representing a C++ source code. Your task is to write a function that removes all comments from the source code, including both single-line (`//`) and multi-line (`/* ... */`) comments. The function should return the cleaned source code as a string.

**Input:**
- A string `cpp_code` representing the C++ source code.

**Output:**
- A string representing the C++ source code with all comments removed.

**Sample Input:**
```cpp
#include <iostream>
/* This is a multi-line comment */
using namespace std;
int main() {
// This is a single-line comment
cout << "Hello, World!";
return 0;
}
```

**Sample Output:**
```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
cout << "Hello, World!";
return 0;
}
```
Your code should pass these tests:

assert remove_comments("// Single line comment") == ""
assert remove_comments("/* Multi-line comment */") == ""
assert remove_comments("int x = 10; // Initialize x") == "int x = 10; "
assert remove_comments("/* Start of comment\nEnd of comment */ int y = 20;") == " int y = 20;"
assert remove_comments("int z = 30; /* Mid-comment */ int w = 40;") == "int z = 30;  int w = 40;"
assert remove_comments("/* Comment at the start */ #include <iostream>") == " #include <iostream>"
assert remove_comments("#include <iostream> /* Comment at the end */") == "#include <iostream> "
assert remove_comments("int main() {\n// Single line comment\nreturn 0;\n}") == "int main() {\n\nreturn 0;\n}"
assert remove_comments("int main() {\n/* Multi-line\ncomment */\nreturn 0;\n}") == "int main() {\n\nreturn 0;\n}"
assert remove_comments("int a = 50; // End of line comment\n/* Multi-line comment\nthat spans multiple lines */") == "int a = 50; \n"
 You should submit your final solution in the following format: ```python

```

